{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794914925955,"sessionID":"ses_e16be6397ffeTX69h5hAKoGVW8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"6e370225-06f4-9ff8-b8ac-6da1002cb537_0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py","offset":1,"limit":240},"output":"<path>/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"The bank statement formats ledgerly reads, one reader per bank.\n2: \n3: Every reader takes the rows of a CSV file (as dictionaries, with the 1-based file line number) and\n4: yields ``Transaction`` objects for one account. Formats:\n5: \n6: - ``generic``: ``date,amount,currency,description,counterparty,iban`` with a decimal point and a\n7:   sign (``-12.50``, ``+1250.00``).\n8: - ``ing``: ING's export: ``Datum`` (YYYYMMDD), ``Naam / Omschrijving``, ``Tegenrekening``,\n9:   ``Af Bij`` (``Af``: money out, ``Bij``: money in), ``Bedrag (EUR)`` (always positive, decimal\n10:   comma), ``Mededelingen``.\n11: - ``rabo``: Rabobank's export: ``Datum`` (YYYY-MM-DD), ``Bedrag`` (signed, decimal comma, thousands\n12:   dots: ``-12,50``, ``+1.250,00``), ``Munt``, ``Naam tegenpartij``, ``Tegenrekening IBAN/BBAN``,\n13:   ``Omschrijving-1``. Balance lines (``Saldo ...``) carry no amount and are skipped.\n14: \"\"\"\n15: \n16: from __future__ import annotations\n17: \n18: import re\n19: from collections.abc import Callable, Iterable, Iterator\n20: from decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\n21: \n22: from ledgerly.core.errors import ImportError_\n23: from ledgerly.core.transactions import Transaction\n24: from ledgerly.util.dates import parse_bank_date\n25: from ledgerly.util.text import squash, strip_reference\n26: \n27: Row = tuple[int, dict[str, str]]\n28: Reader = Callable[[Iterable[Row], str, str], Iterator[Transaction]]\n29: \n30: # 1.234,56 or 12,50 with an optional minus: how Dutch banks write amounts.\n31: EURO_AMOUNT = re.compile(r\"^-?(\\d{1,3}(\\.\\d{3})+|\\d+),\\d{2}$\")\n32: \n33: \n34: def parse_amount(text: str, *, decimal_comma: bool) -> Decimal | None:\n35:     \"\"\"The amount in a statement cell, or ``None`` when the cell holds no amount.\n36: \n37:     ``decimal_comma``: ``1.234,56`` (Dutch banks); otherwise ``1234.56``.\n38:     \"\"\"\n39: \n40:     cleaned = text.strip().replace(\" \", \"\").replace(\" \", \"\")\n41:     if not cleaned:\n42:         return None\n43:     if decimal_comma:\n44:         if not EURO_AMOUNT.match(cleaned):\n45:             return None\n46:         return Decimal(cleaned.replace(\".\", \"\").replace(\",\", \".\"))\n47:     try:\n48:         value = Decimal(cleaned.replace(\",\", \"\"))\n49:     except InvalidOperation:\n50:         return None\n51:     return value if value.is_finite() else None\n52: \n53: \n54: def _field(row: dict[str, str], name: str, source: str, line: int) -> str:\n55:     if name not in row or row[name] is None:\n56:         raise ImportError_(f\"missing column {name!r}\", source=source, line=line)\n57:     return row[name]\n58: \n59: \n60: def _date(text: str, source: str, line: int, formats: tuple[str, ...]):  # noqa: ANN202\n61:     try:\n62:         return parse_bank_date(text, formats=formats)\n63:     except ValueError as exc:\n64:         raise ImportError_(str(exc), source=source, line=line) from None\n65: \n66: \n67: def read_generic(rows: Iterable[Row], account: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n68:     for line, row in rows:\n69:         amount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"amount\", source, line), decimal_comma=False)\n70:         if amount is None:\n71:             raise ImportError_(f\"cannot read the amount {row['amount']!r}\", source=source, line=line)\n72:         yield Transaction(\n73:             account=account,\n74:             booked=_date(_field(row, \"date\", source, line), source, line, (\"%Y-%m-%d\",)),\n75:             amount=amount,\n76:             currency=(row.get(\"currency\") or \"EUR\").strip().upper(),\n77:             description=squash(row.get(\"description\", \"\")),\n78:             counterparty=squash(row.get(\"counterparty\", \"\")),\n79:             counter_iban=(row.get(\"iban\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n80:             source=f\"{source}:{line}\",\n81:         )\n82: \n83: \n84: def read_ing(rows: Iterable[Row], account: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n85:     for line, row in rows:\n86:         amount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"Bedrag (EUR)\", source, line), decimal_comma=True)\n87:         if amount is None:\n88:             raise ImportError_(\n89:                 f\"cannot read the amount {row['Bedrag (EUR)']!r}\", source=source, line=line\n90:             )\n91:         direction = _field(row, \"Af Bij\", source, line).strip()\n92:         if direction not in (\"Af\", \"Bij\"):\n93:             raise ImportError_(f\"Af Bij must be Af or Bij, not {direction!r}\", source=source, line=line)\n94:         name = squash(_field(row, \"Naam / Omschrijving\", source, line))\n95:         notes = strip_reference(row.get(\"Mededelingen\", \"\"))\n96:         yield Transaction(\n97:             account=account,\n98:             booked=_date(_field(row, \"Datum\", source, line), source, line, (\"%Y%m%d\",)),\n99:             amount=-amount if direction == \"Af\" else amount,\n100:             currency=\"EUR\",\n101:             description=f\"{name} {notes}\".strip(),\n102:             counterparty=name,\n103:             counter_iban=(row.get(\"Tegenrekening\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n104:             source=f\"{source}:{line}\",\n105:         )\n106: \n107: \n108: def _is_balance_line(row: dict[str, str]) -> bool:\n109:     return (row.get(\"Omschrijving-1\") or \"\").strip().lower().startswith(\"saldo\")\n110: \n111: \n112: def read_rabo(rows: Iterable[Row], account: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n113:     for line, row in rows:\n114:         amount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"Bedrag\", source, line), decimal_comma=True)\n115:         if amount is None and _is_balance_line(row):\n116:             continue\n117:         yield Transaction(\n118:             account=account,\n119:             booked=_date(_field(row, \"Datum\", source, line), source, line, (\"%Y-%m-%d\",)),\n120:             amount=amount,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n121:             currency=(row.get(\"Munt\") or \"EUR\").strip().upper(),\n122:             description=strip_reference(row.get(\"Omschrijving-1\", \"\")),\n123:             counterparty=squash(row.get(\"Naam tegenpartij\", \"\")),\n124:             counter_iban=(row.get(\"Tegenrekening IBAN/BBAN\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n125:             source=f\"{source}:{line}\",\n126:         )\n127: \n128: \n129: READERS: dict[str, Reader] = {\"generic\": read_generic, \"ing\": read_ing, \"rabo\": read_rabo}\n130: DELIMITERS = {\"generic\": \",\", \"ing\": \";\", \"rabo\": \",\"}\n\n(End of file - total 130 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\"\"\"The bank statement formats ledgerly reads, one reader per bank.\n\nEvery reader takes the rows of a CSV file (as dictionaries, with the 1-based file line number) and\nyields ``Transaction`` objects for one account. Formats:\n\n- ``generic``: ``date,amount,currency,description,counterparty,iban`` with a decimal point and a\n  sign (``-12.50``, ``+1250.00``).\n- ``ing``: ING's export: ``Datum`` (YYYYMMDD), ``Naam / Omschrijving``, ``Tegenrekening``,\n  ``Af Bij`` (``Af``: money out, ``Bij``: money in), ``Bedrag (EUR)`` (always positive, decimal\n  comma), ``Mededelingen``.\n- ``rabo``: Rabobank's export: ``Datum`` (YYYY-MM-DD), ``Bedrag`` (signed, decimal comma, thousands\n  dots: ``-12,50``, ``+1.250,00``), ``Munt``, ``Naam tegenpartij``, ``Tegenrekening IBAN/BBAN``,\n  ``Omschrijving-1``. Balance lines (``Saldo ...``) carry no amount and are skipped.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom collections.abc import Callable, Iterable, Iterator\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py","text":"\"\"\"The bank statement formats ledgerly reads, one reader per bank.\n\nEvery reader takes the rows of a CSV file (as dictionaries, with the 1-based file line number) and\nyields ``Transaction`` objects for one account. Formats:\n\n- ``generic``: ``date,amount,currency,description,counterparty,iban`` with a decimal point and a\n  sign (``-12.50``, ``+1250.00``).\n- ``ing``: ING's export: ``Datum`` (YYYYMMDD), ``Naam / Omschrijving``, ``Tegenrekening``,\n  ``Af Bij`` (``Af``: money out, ``Bij``: money in), ``Bedrag (EUR)`` (always positive, decimal\n  comma), ``Mededelingen``.\n- ``rabo``: Rabobank's export: ``Datum`` (YYYY-MM-DD), ``Bedrag`` (signed, decimal comma, thousands\n  dots: ``-12,50``, ``+1.250,00``), ``Munt``, ``Naam tegenpartij``, ``Tegenrekening IBAN/BBAN``,\n  ``Omschrijving-1``. Balance lines (``Saldo ...``) carry no amount and are skipped.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom collections.abc import Callable, Iterable, Iterator\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\n\nfrom ledgerly.core.errors import ImportError_\nfrom ledgerly.core.transactions import Transaction\nfrom ledgerly.util.dates import parse_bank_date\nfrom ledgerly.util.text import squash, strip_reference\n\nRow = tuple[int, dict[str, str]]\nReader = Callable[[Iterable[Row], str, str], Iterator[Transaction]]\n\n# 1.234,56 or 12,50 with an optional minus: how Dutch banks write amounts.\nEURO_AMOUNT = re.compile(r\"^-?(\\d{1,3}(\\.\\d{3})+|\\d+),\\d{2}$\")\n\n\ndef parse_amount(text: str, *, decimal_comma: bool) -> Decimal | None:\n    \"\"\"The amount in a statement cell, or ``None`` when the cell holds no amount.\n\n    ``decimal_comma``: ``1.234,56`` (Dutch banks); otherwise ``1234.56``.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    cleaned = text.strip().replace(\" \", \"\").replace(\" \", \"\")\n    if not cleaned:\n        return None\n    if decimal_comma:\n        if not EURO_AMOUNT.match(cleaned):\n            return None\n        return Decimal(cleaned.replace(\".\", \"\").replace(\",\", \".\"))\n    try:\n        value = Decimal(cleaned.replace(\",\", \"\"))\n    except InvalidOperation:\n        return None\n    return value if value.is_finite() else None\n\n\ndef _field(row: dict[str, str], name: str, source: str, line: int) -> str:\n    if name not in row or row[name] is None:\n        raise ImportError_(f\"missing column {name!r}\", source=source, line=line)\n    return row[name]\n\n\ndef _date(text: str, source: str, line: int, formats: tuple[str, ...]):  # noqa: ANN202\n    try:\n        return parse_bank_date(text, formats=formats)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise ImportError_(str(exc), source=source, line=line) from None\n\n\ndef read_generic(rows: Iterable[Row], account: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n    for line, row in rows:\n        amount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"amount\", source, line), decimal_comma=False)\n        if amount is None:\n            raise ImportError_(f\"cannot read the amount {row['amount']!r}\", source=source, line=line)\n        yield Transaction(\n            account=account,\n            booked=_date(_field(row, \"date\", source, line), source, line, (\"%Y-%m-%d\",)),\n            amount=amount,\n            currency=(row.get(\"currency\") or \"EUR\").strip().upper(),\n            description=squash(row.get(\"description\", \"\")),\n            counterparty=squash(row.get(\"counterparty\", \"\")),\n            counter_iban=(row.get(\"iban\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n            source=f\"{source}:{line}\",\n        )\n\n\ndef read_ing(rows: Iterable[Row], account: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n    for line, row in rows:\n        amount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"Bedrag (EUR)\", source, line), decimal_comma=True)\n        if amount is None:\n            raise ImportError_(\n                f\"cannot read the amount {row['Bedrag (EUR)']!r}\", source=source, line=line\n            )\n        direction = _field(row, \"Af Bij\", source, line).strip()\n        if direction not in (\"Af\", \"Bij\"):\n            raise ImportError_(f\"Af Bij must be Af or Bij, not {direction!r}\", source=source, line=line)\n        name = squash(_field(row, \"Naam / Omschrijving\", source, line))\n        notes = strip_reference(row.get(\"Mededelingen\", \"\"))\n        yield Transaction(\n            account=account,\n            booked=_date(_field(row, \"Datum\", source, line), source, line, (\"%Y%m%d\",)),\n            amount=-amount if direction == \"Af\" else amount,\n            currency=\"EUR\",\n            description=f\"{name} {notes}\".strip(),\n            counterparty=name,\n            counter_iban=(row.get(\"Tegenrekening\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n            source=f\"{source}:{line}\",\n        )\n\n\ndef _is_balance_line(row: dict[str, str]) -> bool:\n    return (row.get(\"Omschrijving-1\") or \"\").strip().lower().startswith(\"saldo\")\n\n\ndef read_rabo(rows: Iterable[Row], account: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n    for line, row in rows:\n        amount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"Bedrag\", source, line), decimal_comma=True)\n        if amount is None and _is_balance_line(row):\n            continue\n        yield Transaction(\n            account=account,\n            booked=_date(_field(row, \"Datum\", source, line), source, line, (\"%Y-%m-%d\",)),\n            amount=amount,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n            currency=(row.get(\"Munt\") or \"EUR\").strip().upper(),\n            description=strip_reference(row.get(\"Omschrijving-1\", \"\")),\n            counterparty=squash(row.get(\"Naam tegenpartij\", \"\")),\n            counter_iban=(row.get(\"Tegenrekening IBAN/BBAN\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n            source=f\"{source}:{line}\",\n        )\n\n\nREADERS: dict[str, Reader] = {\"generic\": read_generic, \"ing\": read_ing, \"rabo\": read_rabo}\nDELIMITERS = {\"generic\": \",\", \"ing\": \";\", \"rabo\": \",\"}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":130,"totalLines":130,"truncated":false}},"title":"ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py","time":{"start":1794914925947,"end":1794914925953}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"We have detailed report, need inspect ourselves to edit. Need be careful scope: user says statement exact includes first line blank \"Saldo begin\"; salary plus. Need fix plus and unreadable atomic. \"Everything works today same.\" Need decide balance lines with amount? User says import must never drop/invent; if cannot read line stop error and add nothing. Their supplied first line \"Saldo begin\" blank should probably skip because balance line (not money transaction). The sample says shortened exactly line first blank. Import current says 3 read 3 added though if skip balance should be 2 added? Their observed says 3 read, 3 added, perhaps current parser does not skip \"Saldo begin\" due exact _is_balance_line maybe expects startswith saldo? Agent says _is_balance_line likely \"saldo \" and should skip? But output current says 3 added contradictory. Maybe sample includes \"Saldo begin\" and current `_is_balance_line` implementation maybe checks `omschrijving.lower().startswith(\"saldo \")` yes likely skip. Their output says 3 read,3 added means maybe actual parser treats blank amount as None and doesn't skip \"Saldo begin\"? Need inspect actual code. Let's read key files and tests README.","format":"unknown","index":0}