{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794914966576,"sessionID":"ses_e16be6397ffeTX69h5hAKoGVW8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"c60bd57d-c66d-903f-9b26-0d2674622399_0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/reports/render.py","offset":1,"limit":180},"output":"<path>/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/reports/render.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"Plain-text rendering of reports, for the terminal.\"\"\"\n2: \n3: from __future__ import annotations\n4: \n5: from decimal import Decimal\n6: \n7: from ledgerly.core.money import Money\n8: from ledgerly.reports.balance import Balance, net_worth\n9: from ledgerly.reports.income import CategoryLine, IncomeStatement\n10: from ledgerly.util.text import shorten\n11: \n12: NAME_WIDTH = 24\n13: AMOUNT_WIDTH = 16\n14: \n15: \n16: def amount_cell(value: Money) -> str:\n17:     return str(value).rjust(AMOUNT_WIDTH)\n18: \n19: \n20: def percent(value: Decimal | None) -> str:\n21:     if value is None:\n22:         return \"     –\"\n23:     return f\"{value * 100:+5.0f}%\"\n24: \n25: \n26: def _line(line: CategoryLine, compare: bool) -> str:\n27:     text = f\"  {shorten(line.name, NAME_WIDTH):<{NAME_WIDTH}}{amount_cell(line.amount)}\"\n28:     text += f\"  ({line.count})\"\n29:     if compare:\n30:         text += f\"  {percent(line.change)}\"\n31:     return text\n32: \n33: \n34: def render_income(statement: IncomeStatement, *, compare: bool = False) -> str:\n35:     out = [f\"Income and expenses, {statement.period.label}\", \"\"]\n36:     out.append(\"Income\")\n37:     out += [_line(line, compare) for line in statement.income] or [\"  (none)\"]\n38:     out.append(f\"  {'Total income':<{NAME_WIDTH}}{amount_cell(statement.total_income)}\")\n39:     out += [\"\", \"Expenses\"]\n40:     out += [_line(line, compare) for line in statement.expenses] or [\"  (none)\"]\n41:     out.append(f\"  {'Total expenses':<{NAME_WIDTH}}{amount_cell(statement.total_expenses)}\")\n42:     out += [\"\", f\"  {'Net':<{NAME_WIDTH}}{amount_cell(statement.net)}\"]\n43:     if statement.savings_rate is not None:\n44:         out.append(f\"  {'Savings rate':<{NAME_WIDTH}}{statement.savings_rate * 100:>14.1f} %\")\n45:     return \"\\n\".join(out) + \"\\n\"\n46: \n47: \n48: def render_balances(rows: list[Balance], currency: str) -> str:\n49:     out = []\n50:     for row in rows:\n51:         own = \"\" if row.own.currency == currency else f\"  ({row.own})\"\n52:         out.append(f\"{shorten(row.name, NAME_WIDTH):<{NAME_WIDTH}}{amount_cell(row.home)}{own}\")\n53:     out.append(f\"{'Net worth':<{NAME_WIDTH}}{amount_cell(net_worth(rows, currency))}\")\n54:     return \"\\n\".join(out) + \"\\n\"\n\n(End of file - total 54 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\"\"\"Plain-text rendering of reports, for the terminal.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\nfrom ledgerly.core.money import Money\nfrom ledgerly.reports.balance import Balance, net_worth\nfrom ledgerly.reports.income import CategoryLine, IncomeStatement\nfrom ledgerly.util.text import shorten\n\nNAME_WIDTH = 24\nAMOUNT_WIDTH = 16\n\n\ndef amount_cell(value: Money) -> str:\n    return str(value).rjust(AMOUNT_WIDTH)\n\n\ndef percent(value: Decimal | None) -> str:","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/reports/render.py","text":"\"\"\"Plain-text rendering of reports, for the terminal.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\nfrom ledgerly.core.money import Money\nfrom ledgerly.reports.balance import Balance, net_worth\nfrom ledgerly.reports.income import CategoryLine, IncomeStatement\nfrom ledgerly.util.text import shorten\n\nNAME_WIDTH = 24\nAMOUNT_WIDTH = 16\n\n\ndef amount_cell(value: Money) -> str:\n    return str(value).rjust(AMOUNT_WIDTH)\n\n\ndef percent(value: Decimal | None) -> str:\n    if value is None:\n        return \"     –\"\n    return f\"{value * 100:+5.0f}%\"\n\n\ndef _line(line: CategoryLine, compare: bool) -> str:\n    text = f\"  {shorten(line.name, NAME_WIDTH):<{NAME_WIDTH}}{amount_cell(line.amount)}\"\n    text += f\"  ({line.count})\"\n    if compare:\n        text += f\"  {percent(line.change)}\"\n    return text\n\n\ndef render_income(statement: IncomeStatement, *, compare: bool = False) -> str:\n    out = [f\"Income and expenses, {statement.period.label}\", \"\"]\n    out.append(\"Income\")\n    out += [_line(line, compare) for line in statement.income] or [\"  (none)\"]\n    out.append(f\"  {'Total income':<{NAME_WIDTH}}{amount_cell(statement.total_income)}\")\n    out += [\"\", \"Expenses\"]\n    out += [_line(line, compare) for line in statement.expenses] or [\"  (none)\"]\n    out.append(f\"  {'Total expenses':<{NAME_WIDTH}}{amount_cell(statement.total_expenses)}\")\n    out += [\"\", f\"  {'Net':<{NAME_WIDTH}}{amount_cell(statement.net)}\"]\n    if statement.savings_rate is not None:\n        out.append(f\"  {'Savings rate':<{NAME_WIDTH}}{statement.savings_rate * 100:>14.1f} %\")\n    return \"\\n\".join(out) + \"\\n\"\n\n\ndef render_balances(rows: list[Balance], currency: str) -> str:\n    out = []\n    for row in rows:\n        own = \"\" if row.own.currency == currency else f\"  ({row.own})\"\n        out.append(f\"{shorten(row.name, NAME_WIDTH):<{NAME_WIDTH}}{amount_cell(row.home)}{own}\")\n    out.append(f\"{'Net worth':<{NAME_WIDTH}}{amount_cell(net_worth(rows, currency))}\")\n    return \"\\n\".join(out) + \"\\n\"","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":54,"totalLines":54,"truncated":false}},"title":"ledgerly/reports/render.py","time":{"start":1794914966569,"end":1794914966574}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now tests. Need decide where and exact imports. Add MARCH constant. Add test decimal comma plus. Add format test maybe. Add ImportTest report and atomic. We need keep test styles. User asks \"Add a regression test to suite\" singular but can add multiple. Desired robust.\n\nLet's design tests:\n```\nMARCH = \"\"\"...\"\"\"\n```\nWould duplicate RABO somewhat. Could modify RABO to include salary and expected values; but existing test expectations then adjust. Better add MARCH constant.\n\nAmountTest:\n```\nself.assertEqual(parse_amount(\"+1.234,56\",...), Decimal(\"1234.56\"))\n```\nFormatTest:\n```\ndef test_rabo_reads_credit_with_plus_sign:\n rows = read_statement(write(MARCH),\"rabo\",\"checking\")\n self.assertEqual([...], [Decimal(\"-1020.00\"), Decimal(\"-64.35\"), Decimal(\"2750.00\")])\n```\nThis also confirms balance skipped.\n\nImportTest:\n```\ndef test_rabo_import_includes_salary_in_income(self):\n book=journal()\n result=import_statement...\n self.assertEqual((result.read,result.added),(3,3))\n statement=income_statement(book, parse_period(\"2026-03\"), RateTable())\n self.assertEqual(str(statement.total_income),\"2,750.00 EUR\")\n self.assertEqual(str(statement.total_expenses),\"-1,084.35 EUR\")\n self.assertEqual(str(statement.net),\"1,665.65 EUR\")\n```\nNeed import parse_period, RateTable, income_statement. This ensures report no crash. Does `Categorizer([])` built in classify salary based \"Salaris maart\" yes; groceries based Albert Heijn; rent huur.\nAtomic:\n```\ndef test_rabo_unreadable_amount_adds_nothing:\n bad = MARCH.replace('\"+2.750,00\"', '\"2.750\"')\n book=journal()\n with self.assertRaisesRegex(ImportError_, r\"statement\\.csv:5: cannot read the amount\"):\n   import_statement...\n self.assertEqual(len(book),0)\n```\nError line is salary line 5. `assertRaisesRegex` interprets regex; use escaped.\nMaybe malformed salary line comes after valid rent/groceries, read_statement list raises before additions. Good.\nWould this test satisfy \"nothing from that file is added\" but book empty. yes.\n\nShould we test balance with amount skipped? Could add:\n```\ndef test_rabo_skips_balance_line_even_with_amount` \n```\nPotential requirement no invent. But then we changed behavior. A regression test documents it. The prompt says \"Everything works today must keep working same way.\" Does skipping previously imported balance amount break a \"working today\" scenario? They might not consider. More tests not bad. But no need perhaps. Current doc says balance lines carry no amount and skipped, so a saldo with amount is unexpected. Skipping is safe. Yet reference may expect malformed amount on saldo to error? Likely not.\n\nAtomicity of malformed line needs only code parser. Good.\n\nNeed maybe CLI test rather than library report test. Library sufficient. But user asks `python -m ledgerly report income`; end-to-end CLI test stronger. Could add to test_cli using MARCH. It will run account add, import, report and assert income total/net. However unit test helper `ledgerly` always expects return 0 and captures stdout only, fine. Add:\n```\nfrom tests.test_import import ING,MARCH\ndef test_rabo_import_and_report:\n write march\n account add\n output import assert \"3 read, 3 added\"\n report assert \"Salary 2,750.00 EUR\"? Need inspect render formatting.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e944dc26001FI60BAIPafLqkL","sessionID":"ses_e16be6397ffeTX69h5hAKoGVW8","messageID":"msg_1e944cad8001a7wzPVWJG5I1sv"}}
